# Bad configuration change (k6/badconfig.js, 8 VUs; FEATURE_LOGIN_AUDIT=true deployed at t = 4 min)

18 runs from `evaluation_results_badconfig.csv`. Blind test for prompt v6: designed after v6 was frozen (2026-10-03 14:28). Every login runs a synchronous PBKDF2 (1.5M iterations, ~0.35 s of CPU per login), so CPU per request rises ~5x in EVERY pod and no replica count meets the p95 objective. The bad state lives in the deployment's configuration: restarts and new pods do not help, only a rollback does. Server-side p95 is meaningful here (the extra work runs inside the handler).

